    description: "Found in DEEP bakeoff deep-20260623-134237 cohort-001 iter-004 (caddy, Go). Caddy's module architecture dispatches via a global registry: 'RegisterModule' populates a map, and 'Context.LoadModule' looks up + instantiates by string ID at runtime. Hypergumbo emits no static edge across this indirection, so the forward slice from 'main()' reaches only 13 nodes and never touches an HTTP handler / module Provision/ServeHTTP method. This is the dominant reason caddy's forward-slice usefulness is limited despite an otherwise strong Go call graph (9441 resolved cross-file calls). A registry-linker (recognize RegisterModule(id, ctor) + LoadModule(id) pairs, emit dispatches_to) would recover the plugin dispatch. Evidence: reflect/cohort-001/iter-004/caddy.assessment.yaml; slice.0.json (13 nodes from main)."  # 572c
